    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0516" n="504" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/4–2646: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-26T19:00:00-05:00">April 26, 1946—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>785. Ambassador Edwin Pauley is being sent to the Far East by the President to
                    continue his study of the Jap reparations problem, particularly in relation to
                    external assets, and in order to do so plans <pb facs="0517" n="505"
                        xml:id="pg505"/> to visit Korea and Manchuria. He will be accompanied by a
                    small group of specialists. He expects to be in Seoul about the middle of May.
                    Please request the appropriate Soviet authorities to make the necessary
                    arrangements for Ambassador Pauley to carry out his mission in northern Korea.
                    He will have his own plane but, if the Soviet authorities prefer, he is prepared
                    to utilize travel facilities which the Soviets may place at his disposal.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Seoul.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d374-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
